        "title": "PATCH \u2014 NVIDIA Hack-a-Claw",
        "start_date": "May 2026",
        "description": "Competed in the NVIDIA Hack-a-Claw hackathon hosted at Baskin Engineering, UC Santa Cruz. Built and presented a project within a competitive time-constrained environment, applying skills in software development and rapid prototyping. Collaborated with a team to define the problem scope, divide technical responsibilities, and deliver a working demo to a panel of judges."
      },
      {
        "title": "FinSight \u2014 ML-Powered Personal Finance Analyzer",
        "start_date": "Feb 2026",
        "description": "Built a full-stack ML application that detects anomalous spending patterns in personal finance data. Trained an Isolation Forest model on synthetic transaction data achieving ~91% precision. Backend served via a JWT-authenticated FastAPI REST API, containerized with Docker, and deployed through a CI/CD pipeline on GitHub Actions. Frontend built in React with real-time spending trend charts and flagged transaction alerts powered by PostgreSQL."
      },
      {
        "title": "EdgeVision \u2014 Real-Time Object Detection",
        "start_date": "Aug 2025",
        "description": "Ported MobileNetV2 to TensorFlow Lite, reducing model size by 60% (from 14MB to 5.6MB) and achieving 18 FPS on a Raspberry Pi 4 with under 200ms end-to-end latency via a Flask REST API, enabling real-time inference on a $35 device with zero cloud dependency. Applied 8-bit quantization and structured pruning to reduce inference compute by 4x while retaining over 92% of baseline model accuracy. Documented all optimization trade-offs in a technical write-up benchmarking 3 compression strategies across latency, size, and accuracy."
      }
